      "reasoning": "Opponent's turn 5, they're declaring attackers. I have Subtlety (2UU) with flash, so I could cast it as an instant. My lands should be untapped now since it's opponent's turn.\n\
\n\
Subtlety is a 3/3 flash creature with evoke {U}. When it enters, you may put target nonland permanent with mana value 3 or less on top or bottom of its owner's library.\n\
\n\
I could flash it in to block if opponent attacks, or use it to bounce something. But my lands are untapped now? Actually, my lands were tapped from casting Formidable Speaker on my turn. They untap during my untap step, which was at the beginning of this turn (opponent's turn 5). So yes, my lands should be untapped now.\n\
\n\
I have 3 lands: Breeding Pool (UG), Hedge Maze (G/U), Sunken Ruins (C or colored). I need 2UU for Subtlety. Let me check if I can produce UU + 2 generic.\n\
\n\
Breeding Pool can produce U\n\
Hedge Maze can produce U  \n\
Sunken Ruins can produce C\n\
\n\
That's UU + C = 3 mana, but Subtlety needs 4 total (2UU = 4 mana with 2 blue). I'm short 1 mana.\n\
\n\
Unless I use Sunken Ruins' colored ability: Pay {U/B} (using Breeding Pool's U), tap Sunken Ruins for {U}{U}. That gives me 2 blue from Sunken Ruins. Then Hedge Maze can produce G or U. So:\n\
- Breeding Pool: U to pay for Sunken Ruins activation\n\
- Sunken Ruins: Tap for UU (2 blue)\n\
- Hedge Maze: Tap for U or G\n\
\n\
Total: UU + (U or G) = 3 mana (2 blue + 1 other). Still 1 short of 4 total.\n\
\n\
So I can't cast Subtlety. I should pass.\n\
\n\
\n\
\n\
