  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Street Wraith cycles for free (2 life) and is essentially a free card that replaces itself, making it one of the best cards to keep when bottoming from a mulligan. Formidable Speaker is a mediocre 3-mana creature that's less impactful.",
      "action_taken": "Bottomed Street Wraith, keeping Formidable Speaker",
      "better_line": "Bottom Formidable Speaker instead, keeping Street Wraith which effectively gives you a free draw and makes your 6-card hand play like 6 real cards plus a cantrip",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "DSV3 Sport",
      "decision_index": 4,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to cycle Street Wraith on Turn 1 with no other play available. Street Wraith cycling is a virtually free cantrip (2 life) that improves hand quality. The hand is slow with no early plays, making the extra card draw especially valuable to find lands or action. Street Wraith is rarely worth casting as a 5-mana 3/4 and has no synergy with Subtlety's evoke (requires blue card).",
      "action_taken": "Passed Turn 1 without cycling Street Wraith, keeping it in hand with no clear purpose.",
      "better_line": "Cycle Street Wraith for 2 life to draw a card, potentially finding early plays, additional lands, or improving hand quality before passing the turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 12,
      "player": "DSV3 Sport",
      "decision_index": 8,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "DSV3 Sport passed priority in their postcombat main phase without cycling Street Wraith (pay 2 life, draw a card). With only one tapped land on turn 2 and no way to spend mana, cycling Street Wraith is essentially free card selection at the cost of 2 life. At 20 life, this is a very low cost. Drawing an extra card could find a land drop for next turn or improve hand quality. There's no meaningful reason to hold Street Wraith here — it's a 5-mana creature that's unlikely to be cast, and cycling it now maximizes information before the next turn's decisions. Additionally, cycling would trigger any future synergies with cards like Hollow One (reducing its cost) if drawn into one.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without cycling Street Wraith, ending the turn with no actions taken in the main phase.",
      "better_line": "Cycle Street Wraith (pay 2 life, draw a card) during the postcombat main phase to dig deeper into the deck and potentially find a second land or improve hand quality at minimal life cost.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 30,
      "player": "DSV3 Sport",
      "decision_index": 10,
    }
  ],
